# Local Git Only

All agent git work stays on the local machine and the current local branch.

## Required

- Commit only to the local repository and the current local branch when the user asks to check in or commit.
- Prefer `git commit` (and local staging) over any remote publish step.

## Forbidden unless the user explicitly requests it in the same message

- `git push` (any form, including `-u`, tags, or force)
- Opening or updating pull requests (`gh pr create`, `gh pr edit`, etc.)
- Publishing releases, tags to remote, or otherwise sending commits upstream
- Setting or changing an upstream tracking branch as part of publishing

## Clarifications

- Local commits are allowed when requested. Remote publication is not.
- If a workflow would normally push or open a PR after committing, stop after the local commit and tell the user the work is only on the local branch.
- If the user asks only to "check in" or "commit", treat that as local-only.
